  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Albania statistics 2018-2020</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Albania statistics 2018-2020</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen &#xe4;r den sista fasen i ett l&#xe5;ngt bilateralt samarbete mellan de statistiska centralbyr&#xe5;erna i Albanien och Sverige. Insatsens m&#xe5;l &#xe4;r att bidra till att INSTAT uppfyller EUs krav f&#xf6;r produktion av statistik och f&#xf6;r anv&#xe4;ndares behov i Albanien.  
Det generella syftet med samarbetet &#xe4;r att bidra till att utveckla ett h&#xe5;llbart statistiskt system i Albanien, d&#xe4;r INSTAT f&#xf6;rst&#xe5;r sitt behov att sj&#xe4;lvst&#xe4;ndigt bygga intern och extern kapacitet samt att producera anv&#xe4;ndarv&#xe4;nlig statistik som &#xe4;r till nytta f&#xf6;r deras huvudakt&#xf6;rer och allm&#xe4;nheten.&#xc5;tg&#xe4;rden faller under resultatomr&#xe5;de 2 i Sveriges strategi f&#xf6;r Albanien och det r&#xf6;r sig om de albanska institutionernas f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrade kapacitet som Albanska statistikinstitutet (INSTAT) f&#xf6;r att f&#xe5; st&#xf6;rre inverkan och uppn&#xe5; mer h&#xe5;llbara resultat i Albanien, till exempel att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra politiken f&#xf6;r att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra styrningen och d&#xe4;rmed levnadsvillkoren f&#xf6;r det albanska folket.
Insatsen kommer att p&#xe5;g&#xe5; i tre &#xe5;r med start i januari 2018 till december 2020, med en total budget p&#xe5; 19 426 710 SEK. SCB &#xe4;r implementerande partner som huvudsakligen &#xe4;r ansvarig f&#xf6;r budgethantering och rapportering. 
Projektet f&#xf6;ruts&#xe4;tter st&#xf6;d f&#xf6;r att producera milj&#xf6;statistik, samt uppdelning av olika statistik per kvinnor och m&#xe4;n.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intervention is a last phase of a long-term bilateral cooperation between the Albanian and Swedish national statistical offices. The intervention aims to help Albania&#x2019;s Institute of Statistics (INSTAT) to fulfil the EU requirements for statistical production and the needs of the users in Albania.
The overall objective of the cooperation is to contribute to the development of a sustainable statistical system in Albania, where INSTAT understands its true needs and independently builds internal and external institutional capacity and produces statistics  that are user-friendly and used by key stakeholders. The intervention falls under the result area 2 of the Sweden strategy for Albania and it relates with the improving capacities of Albanian institutions as Albanian Statistics Institute (INSTAT) to make greater impact and achieve more sustainable results in Albania, such as enhancing policy-making to improve governance and therefore the living conditions for the Albanian people.
 The intervention will last for three years, starting from January 2018 until  December 2020, with an overall budget of  19 426 709 SEK. The implementing partner primarily responsible for  budget execution and reporting is Statistics Sweden (SCB). 
The project foresees support on producing environmental statistics, as well as disaggregation of various statistics per women and men.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To contribute to the development of sustaniable statistical system in Albania where the National Albanian Statistical institution (INSTAT) understands its true needs and independently builds internal and external institutional capacity and produces statistics that are user-friendly and used by key stakeholders. 
The specific outcomes for the intervention areas are: 
1. Management 
INSTAT managers and staff will be better able to plan, organise and prioritise work with improved communication, involving staff in planning, decision-making and monitoring using a coaching-based approach. INSTAT will be considered as a learning organisation and a provider of knowledge of the statistical system. 
2. Statistical Methodology 
INSTAT will have the capacity to produce and improve existing statistics independently according to EU requirement and the European Statistical Code of Practice and to develop new statistics with sound methodology. INSTAT will also have increased capacity in combining different data sources (administrative and surveys) for producing official statistics and have a system for data confidentiality in place. 
3. Information Technology 
INSTAT will have the capacity to maintain servers and back-up systems and to develop standards for communications.</narrative>
  </description>
